[C2] OPTION A — merge the D2D transmit clocks into the $EXTCLK group

WHAT THIS DOES
    Moves D2D_TX_CLK_0 and D2D_TX_WORD_CLK_0..7 out of their own -asynchronous
    -group and into the system group, so the transmit boundary is timed as the
    synchronous crossing it physically is, and cuts the genuine synchroniser
    crossings across it BY NAME rather than by clock pair.

    Clock groups   5 -> 4          (12 / 17 / 3 / 1; 33 clocks, all grouped)
    Clocks         33 -> 33        (unchanged: no clock is created or removed)
    set_false_path  7 -> 9         (+2, both -to 69 named synchroniser anchors)
    set_max_delay   0 -> 2         (+2, -datapath_only on 22 named FIFO/addrsync
                                    hierarchies, catch-guarded)

WHY
    Every D2D transmit clock resolves master 'clk'. build/full-20260814,
    logs/pnr_qor_after_opt_design_post_cts.rep: 9 transmit clocks x 3 analysis
    views = 27 "Using master clock 'clk'" lines, and ZERO resolving to anything
    else. All 16 receive clocks resolve 'D2D_RX_CLK_0' and none resolves 'clk'.
    The transmit group false-paths a boundary the timer can see is synchronous.

APPLIES TO
    ASIC/genus-innovus/inputs/constraints.sdc
    sha256 90b776a92cdd67ffe19db5d8ca8572ddb6cb0c9b179a57a9d8287eba37cc0a80
    (this file is edited by concurrent sessions; if the hash has moved, re-read
    the [C2] block before applying — the patch may still apply cleanly while
    describing a file that has changed underneath it)

    NOTHING ELSE CHANGES. tidelink_constraints.sdc is untouched: the TX word
    clocks' -source is anchored at $WL/user_hsclk and D2D_TX_CLK_0's at
    $WL/pad_clk_tx, both internal pins that re-resolve their master by
    themselves. That anchor choice was made for exactly this reason.

APPLY
    git apply -p1 ASIC/genus-innovus/inputs/patches/c2-option-a-merge.patch

VALIDATED
    git apply --check     clean against the sha above
    tclsh, all SDC commands stubbed so the foreach loops and error guards
    actually execute: sources OK; 69/69 synchroniser anchors and 22/22 datapath
    anchors built; group census as above.
    NOT validated: no Genus or Innovus run. In particular set_max_delay
    -datapath_only support in Genus 21.15 is UNCONFIRMED — that call is wrapped
    in catch with a plain set_max_delay fallback, which is stricter, not looser.

READ BEFORE JUDGING THE FIRST RUN
    This option newly times 1184 endpoints (1003 clk->TX, 181 TX->clk, by
    structural fan-in over the synthesised Wlink). The exceptions below cover
    the synchronisers and the FIFO/address-sync payload; roughly 200 further
    endpoints are neither and are genuinely timed. See PART 3 OF 3 in the patch
    body for the acceptance gate, and docs/C2_TRANSMIT_GROUP_OPTIONS.md for the
    side-by-side comparison with Option B.

--- a/ASIC/genus-innovus/inputs/constraints.sdc
+++ b/ASIC/genus-innovus/inputs/constraints.sdc
